+# Saved café shortlist
+
+Scope: user-approved local feature brief supplied by the coordinator. Human owner: Perry. Implementer: cafe_willow; independent acceptance review: parent/reviewer. Write scope is this app and its local verification artifacts. No commit, merge, deployment or publication.
+
+## Design and ownership
+
+Considered keeping IDs/storage branches directly in App versus a small domain module and one React owner. Chose the second: `shortlist.ts` normalizes IDs and bounds additions; `useShortlist` owns the in-memory selection and persistence availability. Cafe facts remain derived from the existing registry. `ShortlistDialog.tsx` contains presentation and the small owner hook. App wires existing details and one header entry point to the dialog. This avoids a second copy of café facts or selection state.
+
+Store `sidequest-v2-shortlist` as an array of up to three unique known IDs, preserving order. Malformed JSON becomes empty; unknown IDs, duplicates and overflow are dropped and the normalized value is written back. Storage failure marks persistence unavailable while leaving current IDs usable. This session does not automatically retry failed storage. Cross-tab synchronization is outside this brief.
+
+## Throughput checkpoint
+
+- Blocking first steps: traced details from search and story; verified pure storage/limit rules before UI integration. Complete.
+- Independent workstreams: one coupled App/selection writer; independent parent review after source freeze. No nested delegation.
+- Shared mutable state: one React owner and localStorage key. Private browser contexts; owned Vite port 5182. No shared app/database/browser.
+- Smallest safe decomposition: domain tests/module → UI → project verification skill and live proof. Parent owns lead/reviewer duties, so the forbidden-to-spawn worker writes directly.
+
+## Checks and evidence
+
+- New domain tests first failed with missing module, then all four passed after implementation. `npm test`: all nine pass (five existing plus four shortlist/storage cases); latest reported duration 115.056875ms.
+- `npm run build`: pass; latest Vite duration 929ms. Existing large Three.js chunk warning remains.
+- `node .cursor/skills/verify-sidequest/scripts/shortlist.mjs`: passes real controls at 1440×1000 and 390×844, both detail entry paths, compare facts/directions, duplicate/capacity/removal/replacement, refresh, malformed/unknown/duplicate/overflow storage, read/write failure, keyboard return/removal focus and overflow. Raw timestamps/status in `evidence/shortlist/observations.json`; screenshots and Playwright traces alongside it.
+- `BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5182 EVIDENCE_DIR=evidence/shortlist/regression PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH="/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome" npm run test:browser`: pass. Existing story editing/motion/filter/dialog/session/restart/reduced-motion/no-WebGL coverage; evidence and video in the separate regression directory, original evidence unchanged.
+- Visually inspected desktop/mobile comparison, mobile capacity and storage warning screenshots. Warm palette, readable cards, usable actions and vertical mobile scrolling retained.
+- `git diff --check`: pass.
+
+Initial live proof raw timestamps: 2026-11-18T11:05:16.950Z and 2026-11-18T11:05:48.243Z. Host timestamps were inconsistent earlier in the study; no overall elapsed-time claim is inferred from them. No token usage measurement available.
+
+## Rework and workflow adaptation
+
+One build failure: macOS case-insensitive module resolution confused `Shortlist.tsx` with `shortlist.ts`. Renamed UI module to `ShortlistDialog.tsx`; build passed. Self-review moved the unavailable-storage warning into normal document flow so it cannot cover mobile story controls; added a live geometry/control assertion for that path and reran checks.
+
+Read the pstack feature playbook, architect, model-the-domain, sequence-verifiable-units, create-verification-skill, prove-it-works and maintain-verification-skill at coordinator-supplied cursor/plugins revision 93b916d. Coordinator chose the architecture before implementation. Adapted tool/model bindings to the inherited environment. User instruction forbade nested agents, commits and external PR/deploy, so those workflow steps remain parent-owned. Generated verification skill and feature map were actually launched, doctored, driven and cleaned up. Maintenance outcome: changed (baseline harness now accepts URL/evidence overrides; map updated and live-proved). No external PR created.
+
+Limits: Chromium/SwiftShader and emulated viewports, not physical devices or Safari/Firefox. Storage denial injected at the browser API boundary. Directions checked as exact URLs; external map destinations were not opened. No remaining feature decision; independent review remains parent-owned.
+
+Final focused proof raw timestamps: 2026-11-18T11:08:24.797Z → 2026-11-18T11:08:55.019Z. Owned Vite session70039/PID28386 stopped with Ctrl-C; port5182 closed. Evidence, traces and regression video verified present after cleanup. Source frozen for independent review.
